# Rust / Cargo build artifacts (curl-rs workspace)
#
# SCOPE NOTE (AAP §0.3.1, §0.4.1, §0.5.4): the C->Rust migration introduces a
# net-new Cargo workspace (curl-rs-lib / curl-rs / curl-rs-ffi) delivered in a
# single phase. Ignoring that workspace's generated build artifacts is required
# scaffolding hygiene that ships together with the workspace, so this addition
# is in-scope for the migration and is intentionally retained (not reverted).
# Only generated/derived outputs are ignored below; no source or manifest is
# excluded. Cargo.lock is deliberately NOT ignored: this workspace produces
# binary (`curl-rs`) and library (`libcurl`) artifacts, so the lockfile is
# committed for reproducible, exact-pin builds (AAP §0.6.1, §0.8.3).
/target/
**/target/
*.rs.bk
# cbindgen scratch output regenerated by curl-rs-ffi/build.rs on every build
curl-rs-ffi/generated_curl.h
